{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/681664-are-dreams-chimares-and-other-dream-aspects-important-in-your-chronicles","id":681664,"title":"Are dreams, Chimares, and other dream aspects important in your chronicles?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-28T19:24:38-07:00","id":681664,"title":"Are dreams, Chimares, and other dream aspects important in your chronicles?","content":"How do people use dreams in their Werewolf chronicles? There are a lot of references to dreams in the corebook. There are many gifts for Galliards involving dreams, something unusual for a game known mainly for action and fighting. There are umbral domains of Chimares - dream realms created by people's individual and collective dreams - and the Garou can enter them. The totem of the Stargazers, Chimera, is tied to dreams, and Chimerling spirits who haunt dreams are in the game. There is even talk of the Umbra (or at least Penumbra) being the dreams of Gaia, and Garou going off on dream quests.<br /> <br /> But has anyone actually done anything with it in their games, either as players or STs? The corebook as written implies that dreams should be an important part of anyone's game, but I suspect most games ignore it completely.<br /> <br /> I am considering making dreams and the associated setting aspects a more important part of my own game, so I am interested in learning how others have done that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T19:37:59-07:00","id":683759,"title":"","content":"No replies is pretty good information the answer is &quot;No, we don't care about this in my games&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Perhaps I'll end up being a trailblazer.<br /> <br /> For what it's worth, here is what I intend to do in my games.<br /> <br /> There is a spiritually sensitive person who is in contact with the Periphery. Unfortunately, he lives in an urban Blight, and what he is in contact with is the Wyrm. He uses these dreams as a successful horror writer which ends up creating a Chimare of the horrors tied to Malfeas.<br /> <br /> I'll be showing NPC Galliards using their dream Gifts to communicate with certain members of the Flock to encourage them in pro-Gaian activities and to encourage them in certain directions (I dreamed something positive about that woodland. I Decided not to bulldoze it down to build a stripmall.) This is done to mentor one of the PCs and help him develop alternate means to invovle himself with the Flock despite the Curse.<br /> <br /> I'll be running a Lunatic plot at some point, and the only way to save him is if the PCs enter the Lunatic's Chimare and work with his subconscious to accept his wolf nature.<br /> <br /> I do find it interesting when in the earliest editions of the WoD games where there is an obvious emphasis on something the designers intended, but which the actual players never cared for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T01:43:21-07:00","id":684092,"title":"","content":"It's not that I don't care, it's more that I don't have anything to add. I use foreshadowing and dreams quite a bit, but they have to be tailored to the character(s) and story involved and it's quite hard to actual speak in generalities on something that suits only one specific character and/or plot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T01:03:23-07:00","id":685350,"title":"","content":"Yeah what he said","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T09:05:02-07:00","id":685831,"title":"","content":"I use dreams, and as Asmodai said, they are generally quite character/plot specific. I had some Uktena and their kinfolk get injured by venomous bullets crafted out of qlippothic... stuff. Hurt and slowly succumbing to the dark poison, one of the Uktena entered into a Medicine Dream to find out how to heal his people. Unfortunately, while he was in in his spirit-induced coma, other Garou had begun to cull the injured (and tainted) kinfolk, before a cure could be found. It was up to our pack's Galliard to enter the dream realm and help the beleaguered Uktena out. Eventually they were able to wrestle the secrets of health from a recalcitrant wolverine spirit associated with survival and wake up.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 10-02-2015, 12:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T21:00:20-07:00","id":689226,"title":"","content":"Dreams that foreshadow or reveal something a PC's &quot;sub-conscious&quot; knows, but the conscious mind does not is something that can happen (and often does) in many kinds of games, especially any that has some sort of fantasy element whether D&amp;D, Call of Cthulhu, World of Darkness, and many others.<br /> <br /> What is interesting to me, is that Werewolf offers a lot of tools for dreams to be used proactively by the PCs, not just the ST sending a dream. A dream realm exists as any other location to be explored. Galliards have multiple gifts where they can enter someone else's dream, communicate directly with sleepers, or even change/craft their dreams.<br /> <br /> This is a very different aspect of the game than what normally happens.<br /> <br /> I do like the example Laughing Stranger gave of a PC entering the Uktena's dream to reach him in the &quot;Medicine Dream&quot;, which I assume is some sort of collective dream world of medicine men where they talk with wise spirits on how to heal people from diseases. This is going back a long time ago - while there may be only a few &quot;native&quot; medicine men now, thousands of years ago shamans were the only physicians for anyone. I hadn't even considered this, so it's a good example for me.<br /> <br /> What other kinds of extremely old &quot;dream worlds&quot; would there be as part of humanity's common heritage. Of course, the entire Umbra can be interpreted as a kind of super dream itself, but for our purposes, I'm only interested in things that are obviously related to dreams of people. Lots of people wake up from dreams that have given them various insights - eureka moments that allow them to figure our translations, write new books, invent something new, visions of the future.<br /> <br /> We're getting into a lot of Mage Dreamspeaker stuff here, but I think it's also appropriate for Garou to some degree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}